  "cross_cloud_origin": null,
  "description": "This protocol outlines how to extract protein from mouse tissues and running a Western Blot.\n \nIn brief:\nB6 WT or ID8VEGF mice were dissected and tissues or tumor flash frozen on dry ice and stored at -80\u00b0C or immediately lysed with ice-cold RIPA buffer (Thermo Scientific, cat: 89900) containing protease and phosphatase inhibitors (Thermo Scientific, cat: A32965 &amp; 88667) using the gentleMACS Dissociator (Miltenyi). Lysates were centrifuged (12,000 RPM) for 20min at 4\u00b0C.\u00a0 Protein concentrations were determined using the Pierce BCA Protein Assay Kit (Thermo Scientific, cat: 23225).\nProteins (20mg/lane) were separated on a mini-protean TGX stain-free gel 4-20% (BioRad; cat: 4568094) and transferred to 0.2mm PVDF membrane (Invitrogen; cat: LC2005). Membranes were blocked for 1h with 5% nonfat dry milk in TBS-T (1xTBS BioRad +0.1% Tween-20) then incubated overnight with 1:100 dilution of MSLN antibody (IBL America; cat: 28127) or 1:1000 Vinculin antibody (R&amp;D systems; cat: MAB6896) in TBS-T. Following incubation with appropriate horseradish peroxidase-conjugated secondary antibodies, proteins were visualized by enhanced chemiluminescence (BioRad; cat: 1705060) on the ChemiDoc XRS system (BioRad).",
