   {
    "id": 655919,
    "guid": "453E62735A0F4145B19F2F581AAA7254",
    "previous_id": 655724,
    "previous_guid": "69AAEFA8163D4A39B226B9FB9DD3C205",
    "section": "Western Blot",
    "section_color": null,
    "section_duration": 0,
    "is_substep": false,
    "step": "To run gel, assemble gel so that wells face the gasket. Fill the gel with running buffer and make sure apparatus is not leaking. Remove combs and flush the wells with 1ml micropipette to remove any gel pieces. Ensure running buffer is full is the inside compartment of the gel box.\n \nFor Mesothelin and Vinculin blot, a mini-protean stain-free gel (4-20%) 10 well x 50ul was used.",
    "data": null,
    "protocol_id": 14824,
    "case_id": 0,
    "critical_ids": "",
    "duration": 0,
    "original_id": 0,
    "number": "10",
    "cases": [],
    "critical": null
   },
   {
    "id": 655920,
    "guid": "33E4E7640AFA433F971FD88FCEC6747D",
    "previous_id": 655919,
    "previous_guid": "453E62735A0F4145B19F2F581AAA7254",
    "section": "Western Blot",
    "section_color": null,
    "section_duration": 0,
    "is_substep": false,
    "step": "Load molecular markers and denatured samples. Connect gel box to power pack. Ensure negative is connected to negative supply of pack (black to black &amp; red to red). Run gel at 60V for 25-30 minutes and then at 100-110V for 60 minutes. You can judge how far the gel should run by the molecular weight markers. Ensure good separation. Make transfer buffer and keep at 4C (as soon as you start running gel).\n \nFor Mesothelin and Vinculin blot, 20ug of protein (40ul of sample) was combined with 8ul of Precision Plus Protein Standards, Dual Color.",
    "data": null,
    "protocol_id": 14824,
    "case_id": 0,
